ring if another is drawn. Other discards risk breaking potential chows in the T or W suits.\nReason: Discarding F2 minimizes disruption to potential chows (T2-T3-T4, W5 pairs) and avoids wasting a tile that others might need for prevailing wind melds. My hand is better positioned to develop into a mixed hand with chows and pairs rather than relying on honor tiles.\nAnswer: Play F2"}
